{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 7.873,
   "text": "I drive a snowplow over the mountain pass, midnight to six."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.473,
   "end": 15.3,
   "text": "The old driver gave me one rule. If you ever see footprints in the fresh snow ahead of you... don't plow over them."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.0,
   "end": 20.416,
   "text": "Just stop, he said. Wait for them to end. He never told me why."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.216,
   "end": 25.717,
   "text": "Two weeks ago, in a whiteout near the summit, my headlights found them."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 26.317,
   "end": 30.072,
   "text": "Bare footprints. Walking right down the middle of the road."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 30.872,
   "end": 36.675,
   "text": "No cars. No cabins. Nothing up there for twenty miles... and it was nine below."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.675,
   "end": 41.259,
   "text": "So I stopped. Engine running. Wipers going."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 41.859,
   "end": 46.019,
   "text": "The snow was coming down hard... but it wasn't filling them in."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 47.019,
   "end": 52.309,
   "text": "Then new prints started to appear. One at a time. Slow. Coming toward the truck."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 54.709,
   "end": 57.269,
   "text": "They stopped at my front bumper."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.669,
   "end": 61.827,
   "text": "Then they walked around to the passenger door."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 64.427,
   "end": 69.099,
   "text": "I didn't look over. I kept my eyes straight ahead, and I held my breath."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 70.499,
   "end": 74.659,
   "text": "I heard the lock click open. I felt the cold pour in."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 76.059,
   "end": 80.88,
   "text": "Then the seat beside me creaked... and something whispered, You can drive now."
  }
 ],
